#. type: Title =
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "git-switch(1)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "NAME"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:7
msgid "git-switch - Switch branches"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "SYNOPSIS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:15
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\tgit switch [<options>] [--no-guess] <branch>\n"
"\tgit switch [<options>] --detach [<start-point>]\n"
"\tgit switch [<options>] (-c|-C) <new-branch> [<start-point>]\n"
"\tgit switch [<options>] --orphan <new-branch>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:17
#, no-wrap
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:21
msgid ""
"Switch to a specified branch. The working tree and the index are updated to "
"match the branch. All new commits will be added to the tip of this branch."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:26
msgid ""
"Optionally a new branch could be created with either `-c`, `-C`, "
"automatically from a remote branch of same name (see `--guess`), or detach "
"the working tree from any branch with `--detach`, along with switching."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:31
msgid ""
"Switching branches does not require a clean index and working tree (i.e. no "
"differences compared to `HEAD`). The operation is aborted however if the "
"operation leads to loss of local changes, unless told otherwise with "
"`--discard-changes` or `--merge`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:33
#, no-wrap
msgid "OPTIONS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:34
#, no-wrap
msgid "_<branch>_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:36
msgid "Branch to switch to."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:37
#, no-wrap
msgid "_<new-branch>_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:39
msgid "Name for the new branch."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:40
#, no-wrap
msgid "_<start-point>_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:46
msgid ""
"The starting point for the new branch. Specifying a _<start-point>_ allows "
"you to create a branch based on some other point in history than where "
"`HEAD` currently points. (Or, in the case of `--detach`, allows you to "
"inspect and detach from some other point.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:52
msgid ""
"You can use the `@{-<N>}` syntax to refer to the _<N>_-th last branch/commit "
"switched to using `git switch` or `git checkout` operation. You may also "
"specify `-` which is synonymous to `@{-1}`.  This is often used to switch "
"quickly between two branches, or to undo a branch switch by mistake."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:56
msgid ""
"As a special case, you may use `<rev-a>...<rev-b>` as a shortcut for the "
"merge base of _<rev-a>_ and _<rev-b>_ if there is exactly one merge "
"base. You can leave out at most one of _<rev-a>_ and _<rev-b>_, in which "
"case it defaults to `HEAD`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:57
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-c <new-branch>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:58
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--create <new-branch>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:62
msgid ""
"Create a new branch named _<new-branch>_ starting at _<start-point>_ before "
"switching to the branch. This is the transactional equivalent of"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:66
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ git branch <new-branch>\n"
"$ git switch <new-branch>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:72
msgid ""
"that is to say, the branch is not reset/created unless `git switch` is "
"successful (e.g., when the branch is in use in another worktree, not just "
"the current branch stays the same, but the branch is not reset to the "
"start-point, either)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:73
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-C <new-branch>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:74
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--force-create <new-branch>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:78
msgid ""
"Similar to `--create` except that if _<new-branch>_ already exists, it will "
"be reset to _<start-point>_. This is a convenient shortcut for:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:82
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ git branch -f _<new-branch>_\n"
"$ git switch _<new-branch>_\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:84
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-d`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:85
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--detach`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:89
msgid ""
"Switch to a commit for inspection and discardable experiments. See the "
"\"DETACHED HEAD\" section in linkgit:git-checkout[1] for details."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:90
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--guess`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:91
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-guess`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:95
msgid ""
"If _<branch>_ is not found but there does exist a tracking branch in exactly "
"one remote (call it _<remote>_) with a matching name, treat as equivalent to"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:98
#, no-wrap
msgid "$ git switch -c <branch> --track <remote>/<branch>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:107
msgid ""
"If the branch exists in multiple remotes and one of them is named by the "
"`checkout.defaultRemote` configuration variable, we'll use that one for the "
"purposes of disambiguation, even if the _<branch>_ isn't unique across all "
"remotes. Set it to e.g. `checkout.defaultRemote=origin` to always checkout "
"remote branches from there if _<branch>_ is ambiguous but exists on the "
"'origin' remote. See also `checkout.defaultRemote` in linkgit:git-config[1]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:109
msgid "`--guess` is the default behavior. Use `--no-guess` to disable it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:112
msgid ""
"The default behavior can be set via the `checkout.guess` configuration "
"variable."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:113
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-f`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:114
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--force`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:116
msgid "An alias for `--discard-changes`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:117
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--discard-changes`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:123
msgid ""
"Proceed even if the index or the working tree differs from `HEAD`. Both the "
"index and working tree are restored to match the switching target. If "
"`--recurse-submodules` is specified, submodule content is also restored to "
"match the switching target. This is used to throw away local changes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:124
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-m`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:125
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--merge`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:133
msgid ""
"If you have local modifications to one or more files that are different "
"between the current branch and the branch to which you are switching, the "
"command refuses to switch branches in order to preserve your modifications "
"in context.  However, with this option, a three-way merge between the "
"current branch, your working tree contents, and the new branch is done, and "
"you will be on the new branch."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:138
msgid ""
"When a merge conflict happens, the index entries for conflicting paths are "
"left unmerged, and you need to resolve the conflicts and mark the resolved "
"paths with `git add` (or `git rm` if the merge should result in deletion of "
"the path)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:139
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--conflict=<style>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:144
msgid ""
"The same as `--merge` option above, but changes the way the conflicting "
"hunks are presented, overriding the `merge.conflictStyle` configuration "
"variable.  Possible values are `merge` (default), `diff3`, and `zdiff3`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:145
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-q`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:146
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--quiet`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:148
msgid "Quiet, suppress feedback messages."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:149
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--progress`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:150
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-progress`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:155
msgid ""
"Progress status is reported on the standard error stream by default when it "
"is attached to a terminal, unless `--quiet` is specified. This flag enables "
"progress reporting even if not attached to a terminal, regardless of "
"`--quiet`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:156
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-t`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:157
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--track[ (direct|inherit)]`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:161
msgid ""
"When creating a new branch, set up \"upstream\" configuration.  `-c` is "
"implied. See `--track` in linkgit:git-branch[1] for details."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:171
msgid ""
"If no `-c` option is given, the name of the new branch will be derived from "
"the remote-tracking branch, by looking at the local part of the refspec "
"configured for the corresponding remote, and then stripping the initial part "
"up to the \"*\".  This would tell us to use `hack` as the local branch when "
"branching off of `origin/hack` (or `remotes/origin/hack`, or even "
"`refs/remotes/origin/hack`).  If the given name has no slash, or the above "
"guessing results in an empty name, the guessing is aborted.  You can "
"explicitly give a name with `-c` in such a case."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:172
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-track`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:175
msgid ""
"Do not set up \"upstream\" configuration, even if the "
"`branch.autoSetupMerge` configuration variable is true."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:176
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--orphan <new-branch>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:179
msgid ""
"Create a new unborn branch, named _<new-branch>_. All tracked files are "
"removed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:180
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--ignore-other-worktrees`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:185
msgid ""
"`git switch` refuses when the wanted ref is already checked out by another "
"worktree. This option makes it check the ref out anyway. In other words, the "
"ref can be held by more than one worktree."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:186
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--recurse-submodules`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:187
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-recurse-submodules`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:194
msgid ""
"Using `--recurse-submodules` will update the content of all active "
"submodules according to the commit recorded in the superproject. If nothing "
"(or `--no-recurse-submodules`) is used, submodules working trees will not be "
"updated. Just like linkgit:git-submodule[1], this will detach `HEAD` of the "
"submodules."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:196
#, no-wrap
msgid "EXAMPLES"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:199
msgid "The following command switches to the \"master\" branch:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:202
#, no-wrap
msgid "$ git switch master\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:206
msgid ""
"After working in the wrong branch, switching to the correct branch would be "
"done using:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:209
#, no-wrap
msgid "$ git switch mytopic\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:214
msgid ""
"However, your \"wrong\" branch and correct \"mytopic\" branch may differ in "
"files that you have modified locally, in which case the above switch would "
"fail like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:218
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ git switch mytopic\n"
"error: You have local changes to 'frotz'; not switching branches.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:222
msgid ""
"You can give the `-m` flag to the command, which would try a three-way "
"merge:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:226
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ git switch -m mytopic\n"
"Auto-merging frotz\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:231
msgid ""
"After this three-way merge, the local modifications are _not_ registered in "
"your index file, so `git diff` would show you what changes you made since "
"the tip of the new branch."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:234
msgid ""
"To switch back to the previous branch before we switched to mytopic "
"(i.e. \"master\" branch):"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:237
#, no-wrap
msgid "$ git switch -\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:241
msgid ""
"You can grow a new branch from any commit. For example, switch to "
"\"`HEAD~3`\" and create branch \"`fixup`\":"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:245
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ git switch -c fixup HEAD~3\n"
"Switched to a new branch 'fixup'\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:249
msgid "If you want to start a new branch from a remote branch of the same name:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:254
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ git switch new-topic\n"
"Branch `new-topic` set up to track remote branch `new-topic` from `origin`\n"
"Switched to a new branch `new-topic`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:258
msgid ""
"To check out commit `HEAD~3` for temporary inspection or experiment without "
"creating a new branch:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:262
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ git switch --detach HEAD~3\n"
"HEAD is now at 9fc9555312 Merge branch 'cc/shared-index-permbits'\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:266
msgid ""
"If it turns out whatever you have done is worth keeping, you can always "
"create a new name for it (without switching away):"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.adoc:269
#, no-wrap
msgid "$ git switch -c good-surprises\n"
msgstr ""

